LE KING: I will feel encouraged by that.\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: We definitely don`t get enough sleep.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: You feel like we don`t get enough, but you don`t want to get too much is what you`re saying.\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: Yes, and they used to say it was like eight hours, but it`s nice to -- it`s nice to know that around six hours of sleep, you`re okay.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I would take that too. I never get that either.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: All right.\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: How many hours did you get last night?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Four minutes. No, no, four hours 22 minutes.\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: Okay.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: It is not good.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: That is not good.\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: It is not good.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: The schedule is tough, but we love it.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Who is next?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: But we love it. But we love it.\par \par \uc2 My "Talk of the Table" is a dance group from Uganda that just got a dream invitation. Check it out.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Sony Music Entertainment)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: So, global superstar, Shakira invited the dance group Ghetto Kids to perform at July`s World Cup Final in New Jersey. So, get this: Most of the children are orphans who grew up in poverty. Check out this video of the kids reacting to the news.\par \par \uc2 One dancer said, "I can`t wait to show the world what we`ve got."\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Futuremakers/Instagram)\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: Wow! Look at them jumping.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Isn`t that so great?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I love that.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It`s really cool.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Happiness, happiness, happiness right there.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Happiness. They range in age from 12 to 16.\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: Look at them go.\par \par