ttee for allegations of sexual misconduct and campaign finance violations. He also denies any wrongdoing, but earlier this week, one of his Republican colleagues introduced a measure to expel him.\par \par \uc2 Now guys, all of this is likely to shape the makeup of the balance of power up here in the House of Representatives, with Cherfilus-McCormick, a Democrat now out, that slightly pads the majority that Republicans have by just about two seats.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN: And Caitlin, speaking about that balance of power, CBS News projects Virginia voters have narrowly approved a new congressional map that could give Democrats a huge advantage in that state.\par \par \uc2 Now, how big of an impact could this have on the midterms in November?\par \par \uc2 CAITLIN HUEY-BURNS: Yes, potentially a big impact, Matt, this vote was narrow. Just 51 percent of voters in Virginia voted to change the congressional map just months before those critical midterm elections, as you mentioned. But take a look at this.\par \par \uc2 Right here, the new map gives Democrats an advantage in 10 House districts, leaving just one Republican safe seat, and that could boost the Democrats` chances of winning four additional seats in the House of Representatives this November.\par \par \uc2 So no question, right now, this is a major blow for Republicans who are already holding on to such a narrow majority in the House, as we just talked about.\par \par \uc2 But look, this is no done deal, even though the vote happened last night from the public, the state Supreme Court in Virginia is going to weigh in on whether all of this is legal -- Matt.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I`ll take it from here, Caitlin, thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right, OpenAI and its ChatGPT product are under criminal investigation after a deadly shooting last year at Florida State University. Prosecutors are asking if the chat bot crossed a line by helping plan the attack.\par \par \uc2 Jo Ling Kent reports.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 JO LING KENT: Surveillance video from Florida State University shows the suspect pursuing victims with a gun in hand as they fled. Two people were killed in last year`s shooting.\par \par \uc2 Phoenix Ikner remains behind bars awaiting trial, but Florida prosecutors are now targeting an alleged accomplice, ChatGPT.\par \par \uc2 JAMES UTHMEIER (Florida Attorney General): Technology A.I. is supposed to help and support mankind, not lead to its demise.\par \par \uc2 JO LING KENT: The State`s Attorney General, James Uthmeier, announced a criminal investigation into OpenAI this month, arguing that the A.I. chat bot offered "significant advice days and hours before the first shots were fired."\par \par \uc2 JAMES UTHMEIER: If this were a person on the other end of the screen, we would be charging them with murder.\par \par \uc2 JO LING KENT: State officials released exchanges that show the suspect asking how the country might react to a shooting at his school, where he could find the most students and how to handle guns and ammo. OpenAI says its ChatGPT is not responsible for last year`s mass shooting, adding that it provided factual responses to responses to questions that could be found online and did not encourage or promote illegal or harmful activity.\par \par \uc2 CAROLINE POLISI: When you just type into Google to get information on a sort of fact by fact basis, is that different than engaging in a back and forth conversation with a chat bot?\par \par \uc2 JO LING KENT: CBS News legal contributor, Caroline Polisi.\par \par \uc2 CAROLINE POLISI: It is no secret that these chat bots make mistakes, right? There are disclaimers all over them, but the question is, what was the potential extent of the harm? And do they move forward getting that technology on the market in reckless disregard of the potential harms?\par \par \uc2 JO LING KENT: For CBS MORNINGS, I`m Jo Ling Kent.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: With summer travel 