efense.\par \par \uc2 His name is Brendan Banfield. Police say that he tried to frame the stranger with killing his wife. They say that he plotted the murder with the babysitter that he was having an affair with.\par \par \uc2 Are you following all this?\par \par \uc2 Jericka Duncan has more.\par \par \uc2 Jericka, this is one of the most bizarre stories I`ve ever heard. Good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: I feel like every time I stand here, I`m telling you about a bizarre and crazy story.\par \par \uc2 Good morning. Good morning to everyone.\par \par \uc2 The 40-year-old former IRS agent told the jurors that the theory that he concocted, an elaborate plan to carry out a double murder is, "absolutely crazy."\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Brendan Banfield took the stand Wednesday, forcefully rejecting prosecutors` claim that he plotted his wife`s murder to avoid a divorce.\par \par \uc2 BRENDAN BANFIELD (Suspect): I think that it`s an absurd line of questioning that a plan was made to get rid of my wife.\par \par \uc2 That is absolutely crazy.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Prosecutors allege Banfield was having an affair with the family`s Brazilian au pair, Juliana Peres Magalhaes, and that the two conspired to kill Banfield`s wife, Christine, and a second victim, Joseph Ryan.\par \par \uc2 Under questioning by his own attorney, Banfield acknowledged the affair, saying it began in August of 2022, but he insisted there was never a plan to commit murder, testifying that despite marital struggles, he loved his wife.\par \par \uc2 ATTORNEY: Did you love your wife?\par \par \uc2 BRENDAN BANFIELD: Very much.\par \par \uc2 ATTORNEY: Did you want to continue your marriage with your wife?\par \par \uc2 BRENDAN BANFIELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Magalhaes had told a very different story, testifying as a key prosecution witness earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 ATTORNEY: What did he say?\par \par \uc2 JULIANA PERES MAGALHAES (Au pair): He mentioned his plan to get rid of her.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: She claims Banfield wanted to avoid a divorce and helped him create a fake online profile posing as Christine on a sexual fetish website.\par \par \uc2 Then she says they lured Joseph Ryan to the home for what Ryan believed was a sexual encounter. She says the plan was to blame Ryan for Christine`s death.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors allege that on February 24, 2023, Banfield stabbed his wife, shot Ryan in the head, and then instructed Magalhaes to shoot Ryan in the chest.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: Your wife has died.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Body camera video from that day captures the moment Banfield was told his wife had died.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: We did everything that was possible. It was not a survivable injury.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Banfield faces life behind bars if convicted. He is expected to take the stand again today. Magalhaes agreed to cooperate with prosecutors for a lesser charge of manslaughter -- Vlad.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It is an incredible story. Jericka, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 All right, switching gears now, the most famous man ever to play for Bill Belichick, says he cannot believe his longtime NFL coach was not elected to the Pro Football Hall of Fame this month, I am talking about Tom Brady, of course. He says, "There`s no coach I`d rather play for."\par \par \uc2 Belichick won a record six Super Bowls with the Patriots. So, the snub has sent shockwaves around the league.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 TOM BRADY (Former NFL player): If he`s not a first-ballot Hall of Famer, there is really no coach that should ever be a first-ballot Hall of Famer.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Take it from Tom Brady, the man who spent 20 years with Coach Bill Belichick, winning six Super Bowls along the way.\par \par \uc2 TOM BRADY: He is incredible. There`s no coach I`d rather play for. If I`m taking one coach to go out there to win a Super Bowl, give me one season, I`m taking Bill Belichick.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: According to ESPN, Belichick did not earn the votes necessary to make him a first-ballot Hall of Famer despite having the most decorated coaching career in NFL history: Most Super Bowl wins, most playoff wins, and the second most overall wins ever.\par \par \uc2 MIKE SANDO ("The Athletic" senior NFL writer and Hall of Fame voter): I was embarrassed, and I felt that it was a poor reflection on the Hall and the selectors.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Mike Sando is the senior NFL writer for "The Athletic" and a Hall of Fame voter who voted for Belichick.\par \par \uc2 He says cheating scandals like spygate and deflategate aside, the new voting process implemented last year likely contributed to Belichick`s snub. Instead of voting yes or no on each candidate, the 50 members of the Selection Committee can only select a maximum three of the five finalists from Belichick`s category. To get elected, the candidate needs 40 votes.\par \par \uc2 MIKE SANDO: I think it forced voters to be like, okay, do we put the best guy in? Or what about these other guys who may never get another chance? To me, that`s the wrong framing, and it allows for something like this to happen.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, there`s a lot of people very upset about that. Is it anonymous vote? Is it an anonymous vote?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It is anonymous. Yes.\par \par \uc2 KELLY O`GRADY: Yes. I am --\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: You`re the Patriots fan at the table.\par \par \uc2 KELLY O`GRADY: I am shocked. Okay, when you have fans of teams that hated Bill Belichick, is this kind of all-over social media saying "What is going on?"\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 KELLY O`GRADY: That`s when you know.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: I do. I still have that question that I posted to Nate yesterday, which is, how successful would Belichick 