earch for a new position? According to a recent LinkedIn survey, 56 percent of professionals say they plan to hunt for a job this year. However, 76 percent of them say they feel very unprepared for that search, but not to worry, because we`ve got LinkedIn career expert, there she is, Catherine Fisher, is here in the studio.\par \par \uc2 And word is, Catherine, you`ve got very good advice. So, we`ll be the judge of that.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER (LinkedIn career expert): Okay.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But this is the thing. How long is it taking people these days, to find a professional job? That`s what you`re specializing.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: Yes. We`re hearing from people that it`s taking up to a year to find a new job. And so if you`re in that job market, if you`re looking for a job, you want to be as competitive as you can be.\par \par \uc2 So, understanding what it is that companies are looking for. When you look at the top skill, because we`re finding that companies are really skills- based hiring, they are looking for A.I. literacy.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: A.I. literacy.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: Yes, and this is not as scary as it sounds.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Well, it is very scary.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: It is not.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: If that was a qualification,. I`d be unemployed. I`d be the street going "Taxi!" A.I. literacy.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Wow!\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: And this is as simple as understanding how to use it to transcribe notes or to help with your calendar, et cetera.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Okay.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: So, make sure you have some examples, because you know you`re probably going to get asked, how have you used A.I. in your work? But you also want to lean on your network, because another thing that we know is that people are like hiring managers, 38 percent of them say that they give extra consideration to a referral.\par \par \uc2 So, make sure you have a strong story in terms of how you use A.I. and lean on that network.\par \par \uc2 KELLY O`GRADY: What about when you`re applying to jobs? You know that the sort of spray and pray theory you put a lot of applications in, hope that you get a lot --\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Spray and pray.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Spray and pray. I like that.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 KELLY O`GRADY: Is that the right thing? Or should you go for more targeted?\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: You absolutely go more targeted. You want to be strategic in your job search, because we know that the recruiters, the hiring managers, they have a job to do, they need to hire the people with the skills and experience that are going to be successful in that role.\par \par \uc2 So, use the tools available for you. So like on LinkedIn, we have Job Match. It`ll show you with that job description, how likely are you to hear back based on your skills?\par \par \uc2 What I love about this is it does two things. It tells you either A, that you need to go acquire these skills; or B, you might have these skills, but you just didn`t add them to your profile or to your resume.\par \par \uc2 So, this is where you really want to lean in on your storytelling and be strategic about where you apply.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I like that spray and pray. I`ve never heard that before. Kelly, I like it.\par \par \uc2 Are a lot of people spraying over --\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Are you finding that?\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: Yes --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: So, that hurts.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: And this is contributing to people not hearing back because they`re applying to roles that they simply aren`t qualified for.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Okay;.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER: You only have a finite amount of time in your day. Use it strategically when you`re looking for a job.\par \