rial from construction or something. It was the biggest garbage truck I`ve ever seen.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, I won`t go into the details now and bore you, but to avoid hitting him, I I hit a tree. I hit a big fat tree.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: So I`ll let you guys decide, and people watching at home, but it`s a single lane. Usually when you cut somebody off, you go across a lane. And that may happen suddenly, which causes you to veer off the road. But here, you`re just traveling behind this truck. It takes a turn. Maybe they didn`t use a turn signal, I don`t know.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Maybe that`s it.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Or yes, I don`t know, so --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Or that they were going slower than he thought that they were going to go.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes, that`s true, too.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And so you swerve to avoid --\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Because trucks, you never know there is --\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Or Baldwin tried to make a right turn, not knowing that the truck was making that same turn.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Was going to make that same turn. Yes, exactly.\par \par \uc2 All right --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, we figured it out, Alec. We are just glad you and your brother are okay.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: You should hire us as your attorney.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes, there you go.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: We are just glad you and your brother are okay.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: We should them how.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yup. That`s right.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: All right, President Trump says his cover photo in the new issue of "Time" Magazine may be "The worst of all time." Here is that cover photo. The President is not happy that they shot from under him. Here`s what he wrote on Truth Social: "They disappeared my hair and then had something floating on top of my head that look like a floating crown. Really weird. I never like taking pictures from underneath angles, but this is a super bad picture."\par \par \uc2 "Time" Magazine has not responded. I think we`re all in agreement.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I get why he`s upset. Also, you know how much thought goes into putting on a cover shot?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Heck yes!\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: The editors are looking at it, should we do that?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: There`s a ton of photos.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, there`s a ton of pictures --\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: A lot of options.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And you could also, if you wanted to be generous, you could Photoshop is neck so it doesn`t look that way.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: But everyone --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: So, I could --\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: -- like all of us, when we take pictures in here, we`re always like, yo, you`ve got to go high, go high, and you`re professional, and you go way down here. I don`t know.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I understand.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: You`ve got to take notes from the "I.G" models. They know the angles.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: We got you, President Trump. We got.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: You know what I mean?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I understand.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: All right, let`s end with an exclusive clip from tonight`s all new episode of "Survivor." The castaways in Season 49 have been working in three tribes to complete their challenges. Tonight`s episode features an unexpected shake up. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Survivor"/CBS)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: The drama!\par \par \uc2 Catch a new episode of "Survivor" tonight at 8/7 Central right here on \uc2 CBS\uc2  and streaming on Paramount+.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All right, ahead, author, Michael Lewis will be here to talk about "The Big Short" and what`s coming up next for the economy.\par \par \uc2 (ANNO