s.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Like delulu?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I would really like to do my "Talk of the Table."\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Please.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Let`s go for it.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: You over talked mine yesterday.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: If you don`t mind!\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: All right. All right, go ahead. Go ahead.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: My "Talk of the Table" is a follow up story to last week. Remember this when we shared the male hobbies that women find the least and most attractive?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Oh boy!\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Remember this?\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Okay, let`s start with what women say are the most attractive.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All right.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Number five is woodworking.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Boom!\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Shout out to you, Claus. Claus, no surprise, loves working with the wood.\par \par \uc2 Cooking!\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Okay.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Wait a minute. Wait. Wait. Wait. Wait.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Cooking comes in --\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Okay, Vlad.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I`m still going. I am still going.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: What are we talking about here?\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: So, what are we talking about?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: So today I want to explain what I was talking about. You know, you guys, your mind is in the gutter because I wasn`t going there, our friend Claus.\par \par \uc2 Claus, how do you say your last name?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Stuhlweissenburg. Stuhlweissenburg.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Stuhlweissenburg, I only just know Claus. He`s a very talented woodworker. This is a stuff that Claus has made.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Wow!\par \par \uc2 