called this Monday morning an attack, an ambush. The shooter, who was carrying a utility vest and an assault style rifle fired dozens of rounds toward federal agents and police officers at a Border Patrol annex. Law enforcement returned that fire and killed the attacker.\par \par \uc2 Now three officers were injured, including a McAllen Police officer struck by a bullet in the knee. Officials say the gunman, 27-year-old Ryan Louis Mosqueda who had no criminal record, drove a Michigan tagged vehicle where police found more weapons, including another rifle and ammunition. Now this incident is the second targeted shooting at a Texas DHS facility in four days.\par \par \uc2 A police officer was also shot and injured outside an ICE detention facility in North Texas late Friday night. Ten 10 individuals there have been charged in what officials say was an organized attack -- Tony.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Nicole, thank you very much. Another beat on immigration, the mayor of Los Angeles is strongly criticizing immigration officials for a sweep at one of the city`s best known public parks.\par \par \uc2 Heavily armed federal agents accompanied by nearly a hundred California National Guard troops, took control of MacArthur Park for about an hour. This all happened yesterday, a scenario with a large immigrant population. Homeland Security officials wouldn`t say if the officers made any arrests there in the park.\par \par \uc2 Mayor Karen Bass, meanwhile, said the operation "looked like a city under armed occupation."\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: So there`s a phrase, "You don`t know what you are missing until it`s gone." That`s what the folks in Philly are going through right now. Their trash has not been picked up in a week due to a sanitation worker strike, and the garbage is literally piling up.\par \par \uc2 CBS News 1Philadelphia`s Ross DiMattei talked to locals who have to live with the mess.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 MAN: And it is so bad out here, I don`t know what to do.\par \par \uc2 ROSS DIMATTEI: The mounds of trash piling up around Philadelphia aren`t the only thing going stale, so are the talks to bring back the city`s sanitation workers.\par \par \uc2 MAN: It`s outrageous already. So if this thing go another two weeks or so, it`s going to be totally out of hand.\par \par \uc2 ROSS DIMATTEI: The work stoppage stretched into its seventh day on Monday, after the mayor and union failed to reach an agreement over the weekend. Philadelphia Mayor Cherelle Parker.\par \par \uc2 MAYOR CHERELLE PARKER (D) (Philadelphia): The offer is historic, more than 13 percent over my four-year term.\par \par \uc2 ROSS DIMATTEI: District Council 33, Philadelphia`s largest municipal workers union represents more than 9,000 city employees in essential services. They`re demanding higher wages and better health care and want a five percent annual pay increase.\par \par \uc2 GREG BOULWARE (District Council 33 president): Philadelphia is a blue collar city. We work hard, and unfortunately, a lot of us inside the city, not just us, city workers, are experiencing difficulty with trying to keep pace.\par \par \uc2 ROSS DIMATTEI: The strike also disrupted Philly`s holiday celebrations.\par \par \uc2 LL COOL J (Rapper and actor): But there`s absolutely no way that I could perform across a picket line.\par \par \uc2 ROSS DIMATTEI: After LL Cool J backed out of the city`s July 4th concert.\par \par \uc2 MAN: Just give these guys their money, man, because they deserve it.\par \par \uc2 ROSS DIMATTEI: For now, residents are left hauling their own trash to one of more than 60 temporary drop off sites.\par \par \uc2 MAN: The mayor, whoever is responsible for this, pay these people. I mean, pay them what they need and let them do their job.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 ROSS DIMATTEI: And negotiations between the city and the Union are expected to resume later today, the city has obtained court orders requiring some essential workers back