bsolutely.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: We`ve got one in pizza.\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: Absolutely. So this frozen pizza is from a company called PORTA. It is a Roman style pizza, which means that the dough is nice and crispy. I wish it was hot for you.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I do, too.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: It`s --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But I have to say it`s good cold, too.\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: It`s delicious.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I am going to put this on the thing --\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Totally --\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: We tested over -- we tested over 15 new frozen pizzas, and the winner was decidedly the most Italian. The dough is made with Italian wheat.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: It`s good.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: What?\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: Italian olive oil.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Okay.\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: And some Marzano tomatoes. I love the pepperoni, because it`s a little spicy, but not too salty.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: It`s really good. Yes, there are a lot of vegetarians watching you right now.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: As we slobber down --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I`m clearly not one of them. But for the vegetarians, what did you find?\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: It is really great news, because we have a 365 \uc2 Whole Foods Market\uc2  falafel burger. It`s a great option for anyone that`s looking for something that`s dairy free, vegan or vegetarian. It`s made with chickpeas, lots of vegetables, lots of spices and herbs.\par \par \uc2 Here`s a tip from our experts.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: Cook the patties.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Go for it.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: You`ve got the next question.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Okay, you`ve got enough question. you eat.\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: Cook the patties in an air fryer so that they get nice and crispy.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: In the air fryer.\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: In the air fryer.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Okay, so when it came to the refrigerated section, there was one dip that was very popular. And I love dips because my daughter loves dips now. Everything is like, dip, dip. Want dip, want dip. So talk to me.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: So, Celine -- Celine, by the way, how old is Celine?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Two.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: So, she`s influencing your eating habits?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Absolutely, because I wasn`t a big hummus and dip guy, and now I am, so --\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: Well, this hummus is from Ithaca Hummus. It`s my new favorite brand. You actually get to try it with another winner. This hummus is creamy. You can taste of fresh lime juice.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Oh, yes.\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: It has a little heat from the jalapeno. And this bread is a flat bread that you`re trying it with.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Wow.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Wow.\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: Isn`t it delicious?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: It is delicious.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Myo, I see a pasta here. What can you tell us about that?\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: So the pasta -- these are two winners in one bite. Every --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: How so? How so?\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: So every home cook needs a jar of pasta in the pantry and this one is from a company called Sauce. It has lots of grated parmesan cheese, a little cream, so it`s technically a pink sauce, and you`re trying it with a chunky corkscrew pasta from a company called RUMMO. They`re 175-year-old Italian pasta company. Our testers were so impressed with the texture and the quality of the pasta.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Every --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: The judges did a good job.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes, they did.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: They`re the best.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Everything is absolutely delicious.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Really good. Really good.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Myo Quinn, always great to have you. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 MYO QUINN: Thank you for having me.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Really good.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Three-time Emmy winner, Uzo Aduba is here. Coming up, she will share her new murder mystery series, it is called "The Residence." And how it involved becoming a birder. Yes, a birder.\par \par \uc2 We`ll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Our next guest is not one, not two, but three-time Emmy-winning actor -- did you get that part -- we`re talking about Uzo Aduba, who is calling her latest character, fearless and lethal. That`s quite a combo.\par \par \uc2 Aduba stars in the new \uc2 Netflix\uc2  murder mystery series, "The Residence." Shonda Rhimes is an executive producer, and Aduba plays, listen to this name, Cordelia Cupp. Who is she? She`s the best detective in the world. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 She`s called in to investigate every person at the White House after a mysterious death during a State Dinner, and she is reluctantly paired with an \uc2 FBI\uc2  agent. What could go wrong? Here`s a look.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "The Residence"/Netflix)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: We are happy to say that, Uzo --\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Great scene.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: -- Aduba -- it is -- joins us now.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It is so good.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Congratulations to you.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Welcome.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA ("The Residence" actor): Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Number one on the call sheet. We`ll talk about that in a little bit later, but we showed a clip earlier of you as Crazy Eyes.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I want to talk to you about that, too, but I can say bye-bye, Crazy Eyes, hello to Cordelia Cupp.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: What do you like about her character? Number one, you are so good.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Just allow me to gush a minute.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: You were so good in this role. It`s so unexpected, and you just nail it. What did you like about her character? Tell us about her.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Oh, I loved her quirky little behaviors.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: She comes to cases in a way we`ve never seen a detective come to a case before, you know.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "The Residence"/Netflix)\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: She`s a birder as well.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: A birder.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: So, yes. So she brings some of that with her to her detective work. She`s excellent at her job.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: And she loves it.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And she takes no prisoners. She has a reputation for solving the unsolvable crimes.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: That`s exactly right.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And part of the dialogue, to me, that`s so fascinating is that you have no dialogue where you`re questioning somebody, but you don`t ask them a single question. It`s your expressions that you use.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And the way that you move your body.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Was this hard to do for you?\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: It was. But you know, it`s realizing that she doesn`t want to give anything away.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Away.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: She doesn`t want --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: She doesn`t.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: No, and she doesn`t. She keeps a straight face the whole time. She doesn`t want to let anything on her face indicate to her person of interest she says --\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "The Residence"/Netflix)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Her person of interest.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Person of interest to start moving in a direction that she doesn`t want them to.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: So --\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Go ahead, Tony. I was going to say you talked about being a birder in this role. You actually spent some time with the birding community, of which my wife and a lot of people on the show actually --\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: -- are birders.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Vlad, you`re a birder?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: We became birders during the pandemic like a lot of people in New York. What? Right?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Tony, every day, we learn something new about Vlad Duthiers. You and your wife are birders?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: I was photographed by AARP for the birding issue.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: No?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes, I was.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Amazing.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Okay.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Sorry, sorry, sorry.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It`s all right, so go ahead, tell me what it was like when you discovered the world of birding, and how it applies to Cordelia?\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Okay, I have to tell you, I hadn`t thought of birding before going birding, if I am being really honest, but I went, and I have to tell you, it`s really relaxing.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Is it?\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: It is really relaxing.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Thank you, Gayle.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: It`s not boring?\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: I didn`t -- let`s not lose ourselves, but it was -- it was really -- we`re saying relaxing. It was very relaxing. I would -- I would liken it maybe to fishing.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Oh.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: You know?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Okay.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Just waiting.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: What would be a hobby that you have, that you would genuinely pursue?\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: I -- you know, I use some knit a lot.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I like that.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Which probably some might put in the birding category.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: I was going to throw in shade.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Wow. Wow.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: We were saying it`s a Shonda Rhimes production. So automatically, I think that you go into thinking, I know it`s going to be good, but you never know. Did you know her before? And what did it mean to get a call from her? Her people?\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Yes, no, I didn`t know her personally before. I knew her work, incredible -- I was a huge, huge Shonda Rhimes fan. I did not miss a Thursday with "Scandal." I`ve watched it twice.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Twice. Whoa.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: That was my jam. Yes. I`m a true fan. You know, that was my show and just like Cordelia Cupp, is the best detective in the world, Shonda Rhimes is one of our best.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: In the television world, and it was just a real honor when that call came. I almost didn`t even need to read the script. It was a yes for me right away, you know?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: You`ve got a one-year-old daughter. You just celebrated her birthday. You said that she has been critical to helping you --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Oh, there she is --\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: -- find your inner peace. Oh my gosh.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Can you describe before that then, you weren`t able to land that inner peace?\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: Yes, you know, I think for me, there were so many things outside of myself, whether it`s my job, just trying to connect or land fulfillment.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA: And not that those things weren`t fulfilling. I love my job