ar \par \uc2 REMI BATEMAN: It`s for you.\par \par \uc2 DAVID BEGNAUD: Remi brought Taj a special gift.\par \par \uc2 TYRAUN "TAJ" JOHNSON: Thank you, Remi.\par \par \uc2 DAVID BEGNAUD: Remember that lemonade they were selling?\par \par \uc2 REMI BATEMAN: You trade me lemonade for your robot arm.\par \par \uc2 TYRAUN "TAJ" JOHNSON: Thank you, Remi.\par \par \uc2 REMI BATEMAN: You`re welcome, Taj.\par \par \uc2 DAVID BEGNAUD: A new friendship forged through the kindness of strangers.\par \par \uc2 The donations for Remi continue to pour in. So you know what she has done? Pay it forward. She`s used the funds to help two more children purchase their Hero Arm, 11-year-olds, Faith from Florida and Gio from Peru.\par \par \uc2 As for Remi, she is thrilled to have fingers that function.\par \par \uc2 REMI BATEMAN: Awesome. I love it.\par \par \uc2 DAVID BEGNAUD: The Hero Arm makes even the smallest things a triumph.\par \par \uc2 MAN: Wow.\par \par \uc2 REMI BATEMAN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JAMI BATEMAN: Look at that, Rems.\par \par \uc2 MAN: Wow.\par \par \uc2 JAMI BATEMAN: Yay.\par \par \uc2 MAN: You go, girl.\par \par \uc2 DAVID BEGNAUD: You know, friends, Remi`s story isn`t just about overcoming obstacles, it is about giving others the chance to overcome barriers.\par \par \uc2 REMI BATEMAN: Hello, camera. Bye, camera.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Wow.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I love that her initial instinct was, I want to help other kids. Right away, with no prompting, that`s what she wanted to do. And now talk about pay it forward. Ripple after ripple after ripple.\par \par \uc2 DAVID BEGNAUD: A little nine-year-old from Bountiful, Utah, y`all giving us that daily dose of inspiration to kick the week off right. I mean, I`ve watched that story 20 times, and I`m wiping tears away.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.,\par \par \uc2 DAVID BEGNAUD: I mean, it is the beauty and a child`s desire to do something that for her just felt like the right thing t