uestions and make plans, because we can`t have this happen again in our community.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 SKYLER HENRY: President Biden said this week that the federal government will cover the costs for debris removal and emergency protective measures here in North Carolina for the next six months. Helene is already the deadliest hurricane to hit the U S mainland since Katrina 19 years ago -- Tony.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: At least 217 people. Skyler, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 All right, let`s talk football, aside from Thanksgiving Day games, I`m not really used to football on Thursday nights, but there was a game last night, and Falcons quarterback, Kirk Cousins, he was locked in.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 SPORTSCASTER: Mooney moving. It is fired, it is caught and that is Hodge, and Hodge is going to take it to the end zone.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That touchdown pass in overtime gave Atlanta the win over Tampa Bay. And Cousins for those keeping track threw for 509 yards last night, only 22 other quarterbacks in the whole history of the League have thrown for more than 500 yards in more than one game. He`s now one of them. That`s incredible.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Congrats to Mr. Cousins.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That`s huge. Five hundred is a big number.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: That`s insane.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: One of the good guys, too.\par \par \uc2 Ahead, the Menendez brothers murder case made international headlines years ago, why a district attorney is now taking new look decades later.\par \par \uc2 Plus, disturbing allegations about country star, Garth Brooks and a new lawsuit. But first, it is 7:16, time to check your local weather.\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Still ahead, this morning, \uc2 NBA\uc2  pro, Jared Butler tells Adriana Diaz why he is diving into a new sport and the lesson he hopes to teach