 Double what he is making.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CHEN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: It`s a bold move. I mean, he is a basketball --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Doesn`t it say a lot about him?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: It`s a basket -- he is a basketball purist.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: He loves where he`s at.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: He wants to try to threepeat, which is going to be hard, by the way, but to turn down the Lakers and possibly coaching one of the greatest players, if not the greatest player of all time, LeBron James.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Lebron James.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Man, I give him credit for sticking with what he wants to stand for.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I do, too. I do, too.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Half of $70 million is still a lot of millions.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: No doubt. No doubt.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CHEN: Very good point. Very good point.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Keeping it real, Tony.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: He`s already got some money, and the second part is like he`s still a young man. He could try to threepeat now and then go on and then coach in the \uc2 NBA\uc2  in 10 years and still do it.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But who is to say if he will get another $70 million offer though?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: The \uc2 NBA\uc2  is a fickle business.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I think there is a lot --\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: It could be over in a few years.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Walk away with your money, you`re fired.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: He can -- he can stay and be a college legend, which I think that`s what he`s going for.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CHEN: A lot of fans are very excited and happy about it.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, yes. Go Coach Hurley. Let`s just say that