********************\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Welcome back to CBS MORNINGS. I`m Tony Dokoupil.\par \par \uc2 Coming up in this hour, are some nursing homes squeezing seniors for profit? Well, Lisa Ling reports on her family`s treatment at one facility and how it doesn`t seem like they`re alone.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE MILLER\uc2 : I`m \uc2 Michelle Miller\uc2 . Our Weijia Jiang has gone a long way from West Virginia`s country roads to 1600 Pennsylvania Avenue.\par \par \uc2 This morning, she shows Vlad her hometown roots.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I`m Nate Burleson. Our nation`s capital has been missing something that`s black and white and loved by everyone and I`m not talking about me and Tony. We will tell you when the giant pandas are coming back to DC.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I didn`t think that was going to be my joke, Nate.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE MILLER\uc2 : That was a great one.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: But first, here`s today`s "Eye Opener at Eight."\par \par \uc2 Jury deliberations resume today in former President Trump`s New York criminal trial.\par \par \uc2 ROBERT COSTA: The jury`s requests are the only clues we have so far into the deliberations as we await a verdict.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  will not recuse himself from Supreme Court decisions after a pair of controversial flags were seen flying at his homes.\par \par \uc2 JAN CRAWFORD: In letters to the Democrats, Justice Alito says there is no reason for him to recuse himself because flying those flags was his wife`s doing.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE MILLER\uc2 : CBS News confirms American weapons were used in Sunday`s deadly strike that burned a makeshift refugee camp in Rafah.\par \par \uc2 SPORTSCASTER: The left side, out of play.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: And a young fan at a \uc2 Tampa Bay Rays\uc2  game makes an impressive catch in the stands.\par \par \uc2 SPORTSCASTER #1: He`s like, dude. You saw it, right? That was sick.\par \par \uc2 SPORTSC