andered. I`ve been personally attacked. My family has been harassed. And my story is not unique, it is the story of many public servants across the nation today, and at some point it has to stop.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: Comans is suing for damages. CBS News reached out to Brad Smith and the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  for comment, we got no response.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I think it`s good she`s speaking up. You know, we see all of these big numbers and all the firings, but behind all of these numbers are people --\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: People and families and mortgages.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, yes, yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: They`ve all got a story to tell.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Ahead, from Olympian to the Most Wanted. We`ll show you why the \uc2 FBI\uc2  calls his former professional snowboarder, El Jefe.\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: El Jefe.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Oh what is it?\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: El Jefe.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Thank you, Adriana.\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: You`re welcome, Gayle.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Spanish 101 --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, Spanish 101 during the commercial break. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 But first, yes, it`s 7:17, time now to check your local weather.\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: Still ahead this morning, makes his mark on Nashville. Ringo Starr\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Gunpowder & Sky)\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA DIAZ: He tells Anthony Mason about embracing country music.\par \par \uc2 In "What to Watch" at 7:47, Dolly Parton`s touching tribute to her late husband.\par \par \uc2 This is CBS MORNINGS. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: A former Olympic snowboarder is now on the \uc2 FBI\uc2 `s 10 Most Wanted Fugitives list.\par \par \uc2 Ryan Wedding allegedly ran a drug trafficking ring and orchestrated 