\par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: Wow.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Whoa.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: Pro tip. Pro tip. If you got kicked out of Glee Club -- grade school Glee Club as I did -- because you couldn`t sing and you need to write a song, work with two of the best people in the business.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But Anthony, let`s not poo-poo what you did.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Those words.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Why do I feel like crying after looking at that? It`s beautiful music. Natalie --\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: Well, listen, Natalie, if you could have Natalie Hemby sing your song, I`d take it anytime. You know, I can`t sing. God bless her. She`s amazing.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: She said don`t be afraid to suck. That definitely doesn`t suck. That was very beautiful.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: That definitely doesn`t suck.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: And very you, Anthony.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That was incredible.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: "Talk of the Table" is next. More music for your morning.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: When are you moving Nashville?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: You`re watching CBS MORNINGS.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Seriously.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 *************************************************************************** ** (08:30 AM, EDT)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Time to bring you some of the stories that we call "Talk of the Table" this morning and Tony, you`re in pole position.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: All right, cool. I`m excited to go first.\par \par \uc2 We are playing a little Old Dominion for a reason. My "Talk of the Table" is my \uc2 Spotify\uc2  Wrapped where users get to see their most listened to artists,